config EXYNOS_THERMAL
	tristate "Exynos thermal management unit driver"
	depends on THERMAL_OF
	depends on HAS_IOMEM
	default ARCH_EXYNOS
	help
	  If you say yes here you get support for the TMU (Thermal Management
	  Unit) driver for Samsung Exynos series of SoCs. This driver initialises
	  the TMU, reports temperature and handles cooling action if defined.
	  This driver uses the Exynos core thermal APIs and TMU configuration
	  data from the supported SoCs.

config GS201_ACPM_THERMAL
	tristate "Google gs201 ACPM thermal sensor driver"
	depends on THERMAL_OF
	depends on EXYNOS_ACPM_PROTOCOL
	default ARCH_EXYNOS
	help
	  Thermal sensor driver for the Google gs201 (Tensor G2) SoC, whose
	  Thermal Management Unit is read over IPC to the ACPM power-management
	  coprocessor rather than a memory-mapped register block. Registers the
	  TMU sensors with the thermal framework so DT thermal-zones and cooling
	  maps can throttle CPU cpufreq / GPU devfreq under load.

config S2MPG13_SPMIC_THERMAL
	tristate "Google gs201 s2mpg13 sub-PMIC NTC thermal sensor driver"
	depends on THERMAL_OF
	depends on MFD_SEC_CORE
	default ARCH_EXYNOS
	help
	  Thermal sensor driver for the off-die NTC thermistors sampled by the
	  Google gs201 s2mpg13 sub-PMIC METER block (skin, USB, display, GNSS).
	  Reads the low-pass-filtered ADC codes over the sec-acpm "meter" regmap
	  and registers them with the thermal framework so DT thermal-zones such
	  as skin_therm can act on board-surface temperature.
